Z||000000||p4n1c||01-10-2001||02:26 PM||||Was wondering if anybody had a scanned fiero emblem, preferably the one from the front fascia.  I would prefer a high quality scan and in TIF or TGA format, but I'll take JPEG. Sorry for being picky.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>------------------<BR>-=-=-=[ p4n1c ]=-=-=-=-<BR>-=[ Come out swingin' ]=-||||reg||5
Z||000001||Songman||01-10-2001||04:20 PM||||Do you want the actual front badge? I borrowed the design of one of Orief's door emblems and made a nice logo out of it. Of course, it is a jpg for web use so only 72dpi.<P>What are you wanting to do? How high quality do you need it? I happen to have the nose badge off of my 88 coupe laying right here on my desk since I never put it back on after it fell off.  Tell me what you want and I can scan it for you.<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/songman_1.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000002||p4n1c||01-10-2001||05:00 PM||||Cool stuff, it will be for web use, but I like to have a higher quality pic, to play with(Just in case for desktop backgrounds, etc).  <P>Umm.  Probably 400x400 or around there.  32-bit TIF if you don't mind. =]  So if you don't mind scanning your front emblem, I would really appreciate it.  You can email it to me(derek@primeline.net).<P>Thanks in advance<P>------------------<BR>-=-=-=[ p4n1c ]=-=-=-=-<BR>-=[ Come out swingin' ]=-||||reg||10
Z||000003||Songman||01-10-2001||08:52 PM||||Scanned and uploaded to my server. I'll post it here so you and anyone else that wants it can download it. The problem with scanning the emblem is the mirror-look on the detail. It reflects the light from the scanner and makes it look kinda bad. But you will at least have something that you can build a graphic from now.<P>You probably already know this, but I'll say it anyway. Anything you do that will be shown on a monitor, i.e. - web page, screensaver, background, etc. will be overkill at anything over 75dpi. That is the most that a monitor has the ability to show. <P>I scanned this at 600dpi because you wanted high quality. All that is really good for is high quality printing. Even 300dpi printers don't need anything more than 75dpi because of the way the dots work. <P>If it were me, I would take this scan and make a good graphic out of it and get rid of the memory hogging original. This graphic is around 650k.<P>Good luck with whatever you do. If you need anything else, let me know.<P>Apparently, tif images won't show here but follow this link and then you can right click and save it.<BR>  <A HREF="http://members.home.com/tnfieros/frtemblem.tif" TARGET=_blank>http://members.home.com/tnfieros/frtemblem.tif</A>  <P>------------------<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/songman_1.gif">  <p>[This message has been edited by Songman (edited 01-10-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000004||p4n1c||01-10-2001||09:18 PM||||Thnx I know most monitors only show 72dpi.  My monitor book says 96dpi.  The high quality version will basically be for my use.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  But for everything else it's been converted down.  <P>Thanx for scanning that, really appreciate it.<P>------------------<BR>-=-=-=[ p4n1c ]=-=-=-=-<BR>-=[ Come out swingin' ]=-||||reg||10
